\Author{Šimon Slanský}
\Title{Volume, Specificity, and Boilerplate: A Decomposition of 10-K Risk-Factor Language and Post-Filing Stock Return Volatility}
\Keywords{textual analysis\sep 10-K filings\sep SEC EDGAR\sep volatility\sep risk factors\sep Item 1A\sep Loughran-McDonald\sep LM-Litigious\sep boilerplate disclosure}
\Subject{This thesis decomposes the dictionary-based risk measure of Item 1A first into Item 1A length and risk-word density (volume vs. specificity) and then into the two LM sub-lists of uncertainty and litigious words, showing that the entire negative specificity effect on post-filing stock return volatility is carried by the litigious sub-list.}
\Publisher{Prague University of Economics and Business, Faculty of Informatics and Statistics}
